The public apartment gallery is rendered from `config/apartment.php` via the
`images.gallery` array. Its CSS uses row-major Grid placement so the visual
order and the lightbox navigation follow the configured array order.
Each gallery item keeps its intrinsic image height within a grid row, so the
hover overlay matches the image even when the neighboring item is vertical.
The lightbox keeps the image inside the usable viewport area with symmetric
vertical and horizontal padding, so close controls and navigation do not crop
the photo. Navigation buttons use explicit flex centering; the small bottom
padding compensates for the optical baseline of the `‹` and `›` glyphs.
On mobile it switches to an opaque black, edge-to-edge viewer with a top back
control, live position counter, native site sharing, and swipe navigation; the
desktop side arrows remain available at larger widths.

## Public header navigation
- The public header (`resources/views/components/nav.blade.php`) uses the same
burger menu on mobile and desktop.
- The burger is fixed to the left, the locale dropdown sits beside it, the centered logo uses the compact SVG wordmark, and the booking CTA remains visible on the right. On the localized home routes, the navbar overlays the hero image without a white background and enlarges the wordmark for legibility; inner pages retain the solid navbar.
- On narrow screens the burger uses a compact 48px control and the booking CTA keeps the shared 44px touch target, leaving clear space around the centered logo; desktop overlay CTAs retain the full 64px header treatment.
- The homepage hero content is offset below the overlay header, with a stronger offset on screens up to 420px; the narrow overlay wordmark is reduced so the hero copy remains separated and fully visible.
- The full navigation remains in the existing full-screen `.nav-mobile` panel;
`resources/ts/components/mobile-nav.ts` controls it at every breakpoint.
- The burger stays at the left edge of the public header and controls the full-screen panel at every breakpoint. On home routes the transparent header and hero share the same top edge; the three burger lines morph into a visible X through `aria-expanded`, and pressing the same control closes it again.

## Guest reporting classification

The admin guest-reporting form and public online check-in share the same
AlloggiatiWeb classification. The backend source of truth is
`App\Services\GuestReporting\GuestClassifier`; the shared TypeScript module
`resources/ts/people-reporting-fields.ts` mirrors the rule in the admin UI when
guests are included or excluded. A single included guest is type `16`; with
multiple included guests, the first is type `18` and the others are type `20`.

# Important frontend contracts
## Public availability form
- Date picker minimum nights comes from `data-min-nights`.
- Date picker minimum check-in notice comes from `data-min-booking-lead-days`.
- Guest capacity is validated in the browser from `data-max-beds`: adults + children must fit, while infants and pets are excluded.
- Occupied dates are received from backend via `data-unavailable-dates`.
- AJAX quote:
  - endpoint: `POST /{locale}/{availability-slug}/quote`
  - payload: `checkin`, `checkout`
  - UI-consumed output: `available`, `total_cents`, `message`
- Public UI shows only total (no technical breakdown).
- A mandatory legal-consent checkbox (`accepted_terms`) sits right above the submit
  button, linking to the House Rules and Terms pages via `route_locale('rules')`
  / `route_locale('terms')`. The submit button (`resources/ts/components/booking-form.ts`)
  stays `disabled` until the checkbox is checked; the server also validates
  `accepted_terms => ['required', 'accepted']` as a defense-in-depth measure.
- The Terms page (`route_locale('terms')`) is also linked from the site-wide
  footer (`resources/views/components/footer.blade.php`, `app.nav_terms` key) —
  previously only reachable from the booking form checkbox. The "request
  pending" and "booking confirmed" guest emails (`booking-request-pending.blade.php`,
  `booking-confirmed.blade.php`) render the House Rules/Terms acknowledgement
  text with clickable links (`rules_url`/`terms_url` params via `route_locale()`),
  same as the booking form checkbox.
- The document name is standardized across the site/emails as
  "Contratto di Locazione ad Uso Turistico – La Caracola" (see `terms_title`,
  `nav_terms`, `booking_terms_checkbox`, `booking_pending_mail_terms`,
  `booking_confirmed_mail_terms` in `lang/*/app.php`) — previously it was
  inconsistently named "Schema di Contratto di Locazione ad Uso Turistico" /
  "...Turistica Breve" / "Schema di Contratto" in different places.

## Public online check-in page
- Route: `GET /check-in/{token}` (no locale prefix — token is the only identifier),
  view `resources/views/public/checkin.blade.php` (`resources/views/public/checkin-expired.blade.php`
  for invalid/expired/canceled tokens).
- `resources/ts/checkin.ts` is the dedicated Vite entry (registered in `vite.config.js`),
  bootstrapping the country/municipality combo fields shared with admin:
  `initCountryComboFields()`, `initPeopleReportingFields()`, `initDocumentIssueFields()`
  from `resources/ts/people-reporting-fields.ts`. `initDocumentTypeToggle()` is **not**
  used here — the "tipo alloggiato" is fully automatic (not user-editable), so the
  document-fields block visibility is decided server-side per guest (Blade `@unless`).
- `initPeopleReportingFields()` scopes birth-country changes to the current guest row
  in both forms. When the birth country is Italy, the birth province is visible and
  required; for foreign birth countries it is hidden, cleared, and optional. Italian
  birth municipalities remain locked to the shared municipality list.
- `resources/ts/people-reporting-fields.ts` is i18n-aware via an optional
  `window.CHECKIN_I18N` object (labels for "comune/città di nascita", placeholders);
  when absent (admin form) it falls back to the original Italian strings, so admin
  behavior is unchanged.
- `window.COMUNI_VALIDI` / `window.COUNTRIES_MAP` are set the same way as the admin form.
- Styling: `resources/css/components/checkin-form.css` (imported by `app.css`) adds a
  few page-specific classes (`.checkin-guest`, `.checkin-badge`, `.checkin-callout`,
  `.checkin-lang-switch`, `.checkin-progress`, `.checkin-submit`, `.checkin-summary`,
  `.checkin-edit-dialog`) and styles the shared generated `.combo-select` dropdown
  on top of the `.booking-form` classes. The page shows the booking's total guest
  count and a live completion count with distinct incomplete and complete visual
  states. An already confirmed check-in shows a success callout and a server-rendered
  summary; editing requires an explicit confirmation dialog and invalidates the
  completed state before reopening the form. The bottom confirmation action is
  blocked client-side when a guest or required field is missing, while the server
  remains authoritative for both checks. Adding a
  companion carries the current unsaved guest fields through the separate POST so
  the redirect can repopulate them. The redirect also restores the previous scroll
  position and focused field; province inputs use the `Es: GE` placeholder and
  client-side casing hints, while the server remains authoritative for normalization.
- Language switcher: plain links appending `?lang=xx` to the current URL (reloads the
  page); intentionally does **not** reuse `lang-switcher.ts`/`/locale` (which persists
  the choice in session) since the check-in page's switcher must not persist.
- The guest fields and the "Confirm & submit" button are one form. There is no
  separate save button: the confirmation request submits and persists all fields.
  Validation or backend errors return to the same page with the entered values
  preserved.

## Admin: pending booking-requests queue
- View: `resources/views/admin/booking-requests/index.blade.php` (table: requester,
  contacts, dates, guests, message, guest-match preview, Conferma/Rifiuta/Elimina
  buttons). Reuses the shared admin table styles (`.a-card`, `.a-table`) — no new
  CSS for the table itself. "Elimina" uses `@method('DELETE')` + a stronger
  `confirm()` copy (irreversible, no email) to distinguish it from "Rifiuta"
  (sends the guest a decline email, keeps the row).
- Nav entry: sidebar "📥 Richieste" (`resources/views/layouts/admin.blade.php`), visible
  only with `manage_bookings` permission, with a pending-count badge
  (`.admin-nav__badge` in `resources/css/admin.css`).
- Match-preview badges reuse existing `.badge--paid` (green, existing profile matched)
  / `.badge--unpaid` (amber, new profile will be created) color classes — no new badge
  variants introduced.

## Admin: booking navigation actions

The admin sidebar keeps only the main `Prezzi` entry for pricing; stay discount
rules are part of the pricing workflow and are not a separate navigation item.
The guest-reporting history and Interhome PDF import are contextual actions on
the bookings index. The PDF import sits beside `Nuova prenotazione`; the guest-
reporting history is placed below the page title as a separate action.

## Admin: payment received email
- Booking detail page (`resources/views/admin/bookings/show.blade.php`) exposes the `Segna incassato e conferma` action to users with `manage_bookings`.
- The action confirms the browser prompt, marks the booking income as paid, sends the guest the payment-received email, and displays the last send timestamp. Resends use the same action after a second confirmation.
- The booking detail workflow also shows the last manual/automatic check-in reminder and the last Telegram summary send when available.
- Admin user create/edit forms expose an optional phone field used for host keeper contact details in guest emails.

## Brand identity (colors + logo)
- Palette lives in `resources/css/tokens.css` (`:root`):
  - `--color-primary: #30596C` (dark teal/blue — headings, primary buttons, links)
  - `--color-primary-light: #4a7d94`, `--color-primary-dark: #1e3d4a`
  - `--color-accent: #c7b772` (gold — highlights, borders, accents)
  - `--color-accent-light: #d9cc98`
  - `--color-text: #1a1a1a`, `--color-text-muted: #5a6a70`, `--color-border: #dde3e6`
  - `--color-bg: #f8f9fa`, `--color-white: #ffffff`
- Fonts: `--font-sans` (Inter, body), `--font-serif` (Playfair Display, headings),
  `--font-brand` (Montserrat, brand wordmark contexts).
- Logo files live in `public/images/brand/` (built from source assets in
  `resources/images/logos/`):
  - `logo-symbol-{blue,gold}.svg` / `@3x.png` — icon only (favicon, nav, admin sidebar).
  - `logo-wordmark-{blue,gold}.svg` / `@3x.png` — icon + wordmark (used in transactional emails).
  - Use `asset('images/brand/<file>')` to reference them; prefer the SVG on the
    web and the `@3x.png` raster in HTML emails (email clients don't reliably
    render SVG).
- **Transactional emails**: all mailable views extend `resources/views/emails/layout.blade.php`,
  which renders the `logo-wordmark-blue@3x.png` logo and inlines the brand colors
  as literal hex values (email clients don't load external stylesheets or resolve
  CSS custom properties, so `tokens.css` cannot be referenced directly — colors
  must stay in sync manually if the palette changes).
- The booking-confirmed email payment instructions use a dedicated, high-visibility
  payment panel; the payment deadline remains inside that panel with a neutral gray
  warning style and bold deadline date/time.
- If a different logo size/crop is needed, ask for a new export rather than
  resizing the existing PNG/SVG in code.

## Admin pricing simulator
- Module: `pricing-simulator.ts`.
- Endpoint: `POST /admin/prezzi/simulazione`.
- Shows full breakdown (stay, discount, cleaning, total).

# Specific UI conventions
- Use `data-*` attributes for JS hooks, not decorative classes.
- i18n comes from Laravel lang files; avoid hardcoded copy in core Blade components.
- Prefer reusable components in `resources/views/components`.
- Mobile-first, with CLS awareness (reserve image space).

# Build and quality gates
- `npm run dev`
- `npm run build`
- `npm run build:fast`
- `npm run lint`
- `npm run lint:fix`

# Quick checklist before changing frontend
1. Verify impact on locale-aware routes and translations.
2. Keep `data-*` attributes in Blade aligned with TS selectors.
3. If an AJAX payload changes, update controller + TS + docs in the same change set.
4. At minimum validate lint and a manual smoke test on home and admin pricing.
